{
  "name": "Dealing With a Damp Basement Before You Remodel",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "It's super exciting to think about transforming your basement, but hitting a damp patch can really put a damper on things – literally! Before you even dream of paint colors or flooring, you've got to tackle any moisture issues. Starting a remodel in a basement that isn't truly dry is one of the biggest mistakes you can make, and it can lead to headaches and extra costs down the road. You'll want to assess the situation thoroughly, looking for any signs of water intrusion or persistent humidity. This might involve checking for cracks in the foundation, evaluating your drainage systems outside, or even looking into interior waterproofing solutions. Getting to the root cause of the dampness is critical. Sometimes, it's as simple as extending downspouts; other times, it's a more involved fix. It's smart to resolve these issues completely before framing, insulating, or putting up drywall. If you're unsure about the source or the best fix, that's definitely a moment to bring in a professional. HH Remodeling LLC has hands-on experience in Aurora and the greater Denver area, and we can help you figure out the best approach to get your basement truly ready for its transformation.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
